3
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.700
Here's a quick tip from someone we love.

4
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.090 line:15%
Hi, I'm Courtney McWilliams.

5
00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.230 line:15%
I'm the founder of MaryMac's Doggie Retreat

6
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.670 line:15%
in New Orleans, Louisiana.

7
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.140 line:15%
And this Gabbana.

8
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.150
I'm a social worker

9
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.520
and I specialize in overly anxious dogs.

10
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.120
Many facilities where you're going

11
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.110
to board your dog, offer daycare.

12
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.310 line:15%
So half their daycare, at least two weeks prior

13
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.110 line:15%
to you leaving and boarding your dog,

14
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.990 line:15%
at least two to three times,

15
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.030 line:15%
that way they're comfortable.

16
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.770
They know the staff.

17
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.200
It's not a stressful environment for them.

18
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.470
That's one of my tips.

19
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.870
When you're introducing your pet

20
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.420
to a new environment,

21
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.850 line:15%
I would say, take them out of the home

22
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.810 line:15%
starting 10 minutes at a time,

23
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.330 line:15%
to different environments

24
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.440 line:15%
to see how they will respond.

25
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.880
What will be good and comforting for them

26
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.160 line:15%
is anything that reminds them of home,

27
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.070 line:15%
like their favorite blanket,

28
00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.910 line:15%
toy, or bed, even their crate.

29
00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.970 line:15%
Because sometimes the crates are their safe spot,

30
00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.620
that'll help reduce some anxiety.

31
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.370
If a thunderstorm is coming

32
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.060
and you want to calm your dog,

33
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.850
you can use a thunder jacket.

34
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.630 line:15%
But if you don't have a thunder jacket,

35
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.520 line:15%
you can use an old pair of tights

36
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.410 line:15%
and use their hide to their trigger points, right?

37
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.343 line:15%
Then they put the neck, the chest.

38
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.540 line:15%
Chest right here and the back, the lower back.

39
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.940 line:15%
You wanna swaddle them, like a baby

40
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.280 line:15%
when you tie the tights.

41
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.360 line:15%
But you want to leave the paws free

42
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.640 line:15%
and the tail free.

43
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.010
Cuddling with your dog

44
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.340
and reading a good book,

45
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.150
not only helps to reduce the anxiety of the dog

46
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.931
but as well as the owner.

47
00:01:41.931 --> 00:01:43.090
(bright music)

48
